# ==============================================================================
# GIT COMMIT MESSAGES — Go learning course
# ==============================================================================

Whenever generating a git commit message, follow these rules:

1. LANGUAGE & STYLE:
   - Entire message in English.
   - Imperative mood in the summary ("add", "fix", "complete") — never past tense.
   - Do not capitalize the first letter after the colon.
   - Do not end the subject line with a period.
   - Keep the first line under 72 characters.

2. FORMAT:
   <type>(<scope>): <short summary>

   [optional body for larger changes, separated by a blank line]

3. TYPES (use only these):
   - feat: new exercises, packages, or course work completed
   - fix: bug fix in exercise or package code
   - docs: documentation only (course/docs, README)
   - chore: tooling, dependencies (go.mod), meta files (.cursorrules)
   - refactor: meaningful restructure of exercise code (not main.go wiring)

4. SCOPE:
   Prefer the course day or area, e.g. day7, day6, jsonparser, docs.
   For dependency-only changes use deps.
   Omit scope only when the change is truly cross-cutting and no day fits.

5. WHAT TO FOCUS ON:
   - Summarize the learning topic or exercises (e.g. packages, visibility, context).
   - Prefer day-level summaries over listing every file.
   - Group related exercise work under one commit message when committing a day chunk.

6. WHAT TO IGNORE / NEVER MENTION:
   - Switching which DayXa() is called from main.go (commenting Day4d, calling Day5a, etc.).
   - That is temporary runner wiring, not the substance of the commit.
   - Do not use scopes or wording from frontend stacks (components, hooks, React, etc.).

# ==============================================================================
# EXAMPLES:
# ==============================================================================
# feat(day6): add packages, visibility, and blank-import exercises
# feat(day5): complete error handling exercises
# docs(day1): add Go tooling intro exercises
# chore(deps): add github.com/lib/pq
# fix(day3): correct slice bounds in exercise helper
